# MAGIC <div class="hero"><div class="blob b1"></div><div class="blob b2"></div><div class="blob b3"></div><div class="hero-in"><div class="kicker">Advanced Data Engineering with Databricks</div><h1><span class="kicker-inline">Recap</span>Databricks Data Privacy</h1><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Course 2 of 4</span><span class="chip">⏱ ~8 minutes</span></div><p class="sub">Protecting personal data across the lakehouse: <strong>who can see what</strong>, how to <strong>de-identify</strong> PII, and how to <strong>really delete</strong> data when a person asks for it.</p></div></div><div class="idea"><span class="idea-icon">💡</span><div><b>The one idea to remember:</b> put privacy into the <strong>platform</strong>, not into every job. Use Unity Catalog permissions, <strong>row filters and column masks</strong> (ideally driven by <strong>tags</strong>), de-identify early in the medallion flow, and design deletes that also remove old file versions.</div></div>
