# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">05</span><span class="sec-icon">🔐</span><h2>A privacy-aware medallion flow</h2></div><pre class="diagram">landing ─► bronze   raw data incl. PII        restricted schema, very few principals
# MAGIC         ─► silver   hashed / tokenized IDs, PII columns tagged → masks via ABAC
# MAGIC         ─► gold     aggregated / generalized, no direct identifiers → broad access</pre>
# MAGIC <ol>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Data classification</strong> scans tables, detects PII (emails, phone numbers, IBANs, names…) and applies <strong>governed tags</strong> automatically.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Tags + ABAC</strong> mask everything tagged, including columns added later.</li>
# MAGIC <li>De-identify in the <strong>bronze → silver</strong> step, e.g. with pipeline code or a UDF.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Put <strong>expectations</strong> on silver, so the pipeline fails if PII-looking values appear where they shouldn't.</li>
# MAGIC </ol>
